# Conventional Commit Template
# Specification: conventionalcommits.org
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types (of Conventional Commits) [Used in Subject]
# - feat: A new user-facing feature
# - fix: A bug fix
# - docs: Documentation-only adjustments
# - style: Code formatting changes that have no affect on logic
# - refactor: Code alterations that neither fix bugs nor add features
# - perf: Changes made to improve performance
# - test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# - chore: Maintenance tasks, build updates, or dependency bumps
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Subject: <type>(<scope>): <short summary in imperative mood>


# Example: feat(auth): add login captcha verification
# Keep summary under 50 characters. Do not end with a period.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Body: Detailed description of what changed and WHY (not how)


# Wrap lines at 72 characters (the length of each hyphen rule)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Footer: Breaking changes, issue tracker references, or co-authors.

# Example: Fixes #123
# Example: Co-authored-by: Name <email>